## Files

**New**
- `src/cljc/yin/repl/host.cljc` — the host-socket seam. `websocket` returns nil (no v2 host package exists in this tree); `owed` states what clj/cljs/cljd each still owe; `adapter?`/`binder?` are the composition gates `connect` and `serve!` check.
- `src/cljc/yin/repl/connect.cljc` — R3. Canonical request-target normalization (dot-segment removal, unreserved percent-decoding, upper-cased remaining hex, `%2F` left encoded, query/fragment dropped, empty path → `/repl`, explicit `/` kept), URL→descriptor, `boundary` (one capacity-8192 medium, response cursor and lifecycle cursor both minted before `attach!`), `open`, `close!`, `reattachable?`, `reattach` (`attach!` + `rpc-ws/rebind`), and `observe`, which translates deposited envelopes through the R1 decoder and interprets only the neutral `:dao.stream.apply/…` vocabulary.
- `src/cljc/yin/repl/serve.cljc` — R4. `serve!` creates the capacity-1 `/repl` service stream, capacity-1024 control medium, 8 capacity-1 offer/ack handoff slots, and the capacity-256 lifecycle medium — every cursor minted before any bind — then composes `ws/make-endpoint` + `dao.stream.serving` and returns immediately. `step` is the one server driver (lifecycle → transport/serving → session adoption → one bounded session step against a single serially threaded shell). `stop!` closes the service stream and claims nothing; only the `:stopped` event marks completion and releases the resolution entry.

